#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/job-interview.ts:19
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"A successful job interview is not about memorizing perfect answers. It is "
"about helping the interviewer understand what you can do, how you work, and "
"why your experience is relevant.\n"
"\n"
"Strong answers are clear, specific, and supported by real examples. You do "
"not need complicated vocabulary or overly formal language. Focus on "
"explaining your experience in a structured and convincing way.\n"
"\n"
"## Prepare Before the Interview\n"
"\n"
"Before the interview, review:\n"
"\n"
"- The role and its main responsibilities\n"
"- The most important requirements\n"
"- The company’s products and customers\n"
"- Your most relevant experience\n"
"- Two or three achievements\n"
"- Examples of problems you solved\n"
"- Questions you want to ask\n"
"\n"
"Connect your experience to the vacancy. If teamwork is important, prepare a "
"teamwork example. If the role requires leadership, think of a time you took "
"responsibility or helped a team make progress.\n"
"\n"
"You do not need to match every requirement. Be ready to explain how your "
"existing skills can transfer to unfamiliar responsibilities.\n"
"\n"
"## Introduce Yourself\n"
"\n"
"Many interviews begin with:\n"
"\n"
"> “Could you tell me about yourself?”\n"
"\n"
"Give a short professional summary covering:\n"
"\n"
"1. What you do\n"
"2. Your relevant experience\n"
"3. Your strongest skills\n"
"4. Why you want this role\n"
"\n"
"A useful structure is:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’m a [profession] with experience in [area]. In my current or most "
"recent role, I [responsibility or achievement]. My strongest skills include "
"[skills]. I’m now looking for an opportunity where I can [goal connected to "
"the vacancy].”\n"
"\n"
"Example:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’m a frontend developer with five years of experience building web "
"applications. I mainly work with React and TypeScript and help improve "
"frontend architecture and automated testing. I’m now looking for a role "
"where I can take more ownership and contribute to technical decisions.”\n"
"\n"
"Keep your introduction focused. One or two minutes is usually enough.\n"
"\n"
"## Explain Your Motivation\n"
"\n"
"Interviewers may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Why are you interested in this position?”\n"
"- “Why do you want to work here?”\n"
"- “Why are you leaving your current role?”\n"
"\n"
"Connect three things:\n"
"\n"
"- Something specific about the role or company\n"
"- Your relevant experience\n"
"- What you want to develop next\n"
"\n"
"Example:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’m interested in this role because it combines frontend development "
"with product ownership. I have experience building React applications and "
"improving testing processes, and I would now like to participate more "
"actively in architecture and product decisions.”\n"
"\n"
"Avoid focusing only on salary, remote work, or needing any available job.\n"
"\n"
"## Use the STAR Method\n"
"\n"
"For questions about past experience, use **STAR**:\n"
"\n"
"- **Situation:** Explain the context.\n"
"- **Task:** Describe your responsibility.\n"
"- **Action:** Explain what you personally did.\n"
"- **Result:** Describe the outcome and lesson.\n"
"\n"
"Example:\n"
"\n"
"> “Our checkout page frequently failed on mobile devices. I investigated "
"analytics and reproduced the issue on several devices. I discovered that "
"two requests were creating a race condition, changed the request flow, and "
"added integration tests. After the release, mobile checkout errors "
"decreased significantly.”\n"
"\n"
"The **Action** section should usually contain the most detail. Interviewers "
"want to understand your contribution, not only what the team did.\n"
"\n"
"## Make Answers Specific\n"
"\n"
"Compare:\n"
"\n"
"> “I helped improve the product.”\n"
"\n"
"With:\n"
"\n"
"> “I redesigned the onboarding flow, simplified three steps with the "
"designer, and added analytics. The percentage of users completing "
"onboarding increased from 62% to 78%.”\n"
"\n"
"Use accurate numbers when they are meaningful. You can mention increased "
"revenue, reduced errors, faster delivery, saved time, improved "
"satisfaction, or more completed processes.\n"
"\n"
"When exact numbers are unavailable, describe a concrete result:\n"
"\n"
"- “The support team stopped receiving repeated complaints.”\n"
"- “We completed the migration without downtime.”\n"
"- “The solution was adopted by two other teams.”\n"
"\n"
"Do not invent statistics.\n"
"\n"
"## Explain Your Contribution\n"
"\n"
"Interviewers may ask about your responsibilities, projects, or role within "
"a team.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I was responsible for…”\n"
"- “My main contribution was…”\n"
"- “I took ownership of…”\n"
"- “I worked closely with…”\n"
"- “The team delivered the project, while I focused on…”\n"
"- “I was involved from planning through release.”\n"
"\n"
"Use “we” for shared results and “I” for your own actions.\n"
"\n"
"## Describe Strengths With Evidence\n"
"\n"
"Choose strengths that are relevant to the role and support them with "
"examples.\n"
"\n"
"Instead of:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’m a good communicator.”\n"
"\n"
"Try:\n"
"\n"
"> “One of my strengths is explaining technical decisions to non-technical "
"colleagues. During our last redesign, I used simple prototypes to explain "
"performance trade-offs to the product and design teams. This helped us "
"agree on a solution without delaying the release.”\n"
"\n"
"Possible strengths include problem-solving, reliability, communication, "
"adaptability, leadership, organization, technical expertise, and learning "
"quickly.\n"
"\n"
"## Discuss a Weakness Honestly\n"
"\n"
"Choose a real limitation that does not make you unsuitable for the role. "
"Explain:\n"
"\n"
"1. What the weakness is\n"
"2. When it affects you\n"
"3. What you are doing about it\n"
"4. What progress you have made\n"
"\n"
"Example:\n"
"\n"
"> “I sometimes spend too much time refining details before sharing my work. "
"I now share earlier drafts and agree on the expected level of detail before "
"starting. This has helped me get feedback sooner and work more "
"efficiently.”\n"
"\n"
"Avoid disguised strengths such as “I work too hard.”\n"
"\n"
"## Explain Mistakes and Failures\n"
"\n"
"A good answer demonstrates responsibility and learning.\n"
"\n"
"Include:\n"
"\n"
"- What happened\n"
"- What your role was\n"
"- What you should have done differently\n"
"- How you reduced the impact\n"
"- What you changed afterward\n"
"\n"
"Example:\n"
"\n"
"> “I underestimated a data migration because I did not include enough time "
"for testing with production data. I raised the risk early, reduced the "
"first release’s scope, and created a better validation plan. Since then, I "
"include validation and rollback planning in migration estimates.”\n"
"\n"
"Do not blame colleagues or pretend the mistake had no consequences.\n"
"\n"
"## Talk About Conflict\n"
"\n"
"When describing a disagreement, explain:\n"
"\n"
"- What the disagreement was about\n"
"- Why both sides had reasonable concerns\n"
"- How you listened and explained your view\n"
"- How the decision was made\n"
"- What happened afterward\n"
"\n"
"Example:\n"
"\n"
"> “A designer and I disagreed about an animation that caused performance "
"problems on older phones. I prepared two prototypes and measured their "
"performance. We chose a simpler version that preserved the main visual "
"effect.”\n"
"\n"
"Focus on communication and resolution. Avoid describing the other person as "
"incompetent or unreasonable.\n"
"\n"
"## Explain How You Work\n"
"\n"
"Interviewers may ask how you communicate, ask for help, give feedback, or "
"manage shared responsibility.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I keep stakeholders informed by…”\n"
"- “I prefer to raise risks early.”\n"
"- “When I am blocked, I first…, and then…”\n"
"- “I focus feedback on the work and its impact.”\n"
"- “I make sure responsibilities are clear before we begin.”\n"
"- “I adapt the level of detail to the person I am speaking with.”\n"
"\n"
"Support these claims with examples.\n"
"\n"
"## Explain How You Prioritize\n"
"\n"
"When several tasks seem urgent:\n"
"\n"
"- Compare their business impact\n"
"- Check deadlines and dependencies\n"
"- Discuss trade-offs\n"
"- Confirm priorities with the relevant person\n"
"- Divide work into smaller deliverables\n"
"- Communicate risks early\n"
"\n"
"Example:\n"
"\n"
"> “I compare the customer impact, deadlines, and dependencies of each task. "
"I confirm priorities with the product owner instead of making assumptions "
"and communicate immediately if the timeline is at risk.”\n"
"\n"
"## Answer Hypothetical Questions\n"
"\n"
"For unfamiliar situations:\n"
"\n"
"1. Clarify the situation.\n"
"2. Identify the goal and constraints.\n"
"3. Gather information.\n"
"4. Consider the options.\n"
"5. Communicate with relevant people.\n"
"6. Take action.\n"
"7. Review the result.\n"
"\n"
"You can ask a clarifying question before answering:\n"
"\n"
"> “Would I be responsible for making the final decision, or would I be "
"advising the project owner?”\n"
"\n"
"## Be Honest About Missing Experience\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I have not used that exact tool, but I have worked with a similar one.”\n"
"- “I do not yet have direct experience in that area.”\n"
"- “My closest relevant experience is…”\n"
"- “I would approach learning it by…”\n"
"- “Although I have not done that professionally, I used it in a personal "
"project.”\n"
"\n"
"A useful structure is:\n"
"\n"
"> “I have not done X directly, but I have experience with Y, which uses "
"similar principles. I learned Z quickly in my previous role, so I would use "
"a similar approach here.”\n"
"\n"
"Do not exaggerate your experience.\n"
"\n"
"## Explain Career Changes and Employment Gaps\n"
"\n"
"Keep the explanation honest, concise, and focused on the future.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I took time away from work to…”\n"
"- “My position was affected by restructuring.”\n"
"- “I decided to change direction because…”\n"
"- “During that period, I focused on…”\n"
"- “The experience helped me clarify that I want to…”\n"
"\n"
"You do not need to disclose deeply personal information.\n"
"\n"
"## Discuss Salary Expectations\n"
"\n"
"You can provide a range:\n"
"\n"
"> “Based on the responsibilities and my experience, I’m targeting a gross "
"annual salary between X and Y. I’m also considering the full compensation "
"package and the scope of the role.”\n"
"\n"
"You can also ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you share the budgeted salary range?”\n"
"- “Does the figure include bonuses?”\n"
"- “Are there regular salary reviews?”\n"
"- “Is there flexibility depending on the final responsibilities?”\n"
"\n"
"Research local market rates and consider salary, benefits, vacation, "
"working arrangements, and development opportunities.\n"
"\n"
"## Ask Questions at the End\n"
"\n"
"Prepare several thoughtful questions.\n"
"\n"
"### About the role\n"
"\n"
"- “What would success look like during the first three months?”\n"
"- “What are the most important problems this person should solve?”\n"
"- “Why is the position currently open?”\n"
"- “What are the biggest challenges in this role?”\n"
"\n"
"### About the team\n"
"\n"
"- “How is the team structured?”\n"
"- “Who would I work with most closely?”\n"
"- “How are important decisions made?”\n"
"- “How does the team share feedback?”\n"
"\n"
"### About the process\n"
"\n"
"- “What are the next steps?”\n"
"- “Is there anything about my experience you would like me to clarify?”\n"
"- “When do you expect to make a decision?”\n"
"\n"
"Use this opportunity to evaluate the role, not only to demonstrate "
"interest.\n"
"\n"
"## Ask for Clarification\n"
"\n"
"You do not need to answer immediately when a question is unclear.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you clarify what you mean?”\n"
"- “Would you like an example from my current role?”\n"
"- “Could you repeat the question, please?”\n"
"- “May I take a moment to think?”\n"
"- “Let me make sure I understood correctly.”\n"
"\n"
"A short pause is better than an unfocused answer.\n"
"\n"
"## Keep Answers Focused\n"
"\n"
"Most answers should take between one and three minutes.\n"
"\n"
"A useful structure is:\n"
"\n"
"1. Begin with your main point.\n"
"2. Give one relevant example.\n"
"3. Explain your actions and the result.\n"
"4. Stop and allow a follow-up question.\n"
"\n"
"A strong opening might be:\n"
"\n"
"> “Yes. The best example is a migration project I led last year.”\n"
"\n"
"If your answer becomes too long, say:\n"
"\n"
"- “The main result was…”\n"
"- “To summarize…”\n"
"- “The most important lesson was…”\n"
"\n"
"## Communicate Naturally in a Second Language\n"
"\n"
"Perfect grammar is not required. Prioritize:\n"
"\n"
"- Clear structure\n"
"- Specific examples\n"
"- Understandable pronunciation\n"
"- Relevant information\n"
"- Careful listening\n"
"- Asking for clarification\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “What I mean is…”\n"
"- “Let me explain that another way.”\n"
"- “I’m looking for the right word.”\n"
"- “Could you speak a little more slowly?”\n"
"- “I need a moment to organize my answer.”\n"
"\n"
"Correcting yourself calmly is completely acceptable.\n"
"\n"
"## Online Interview Tips\n"
"\n"
"Before a video interview:\n"
"\n"
"- Test your camera, microphone, and internet connection.\n"
"- Join several minutes early.\n"
"- Keep your CV and the vacancy nearby.\n"
"- Close unnecessary applications and notifications.\n"
"- Choose a quiet, well-lit place.\n"
"- Keep the interviewer’s contact details available.\n"
"\n"
"If there is a technical problem, say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’m sorry, the audio is breaking up.”\n"
"- “Could you repeat the last sentence?”\n"
"- “I think there is a delay.”\n"
"- “Would you mind if I turned off my camera?”\n"
"- “Could we reconnect using the same link?”\n"
"\n"
"## End Professionally\n"
"\n"
"At the end, you can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Thank you for your time.”\n"
"- “I enjoyed learning more about the role.”\n"
"- “The position sounds closely connected to what I would like to do next.”\n"
"- “Please let me know if you need any additional information.”\n"
"- “I look forward to hearing about the next steps.”\n"
"\n"
"Express interest, thank the interviewer, and confirm the process.\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Answer Formula\n"
"\n"
"For most experience-based questions, use:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Answer:** Give your main point.\n"
"2. **Example:** Describe one relevant situation.\n"
"3. **Action:** Explain what you did.\n"
"4. **Result:** Describe the outcome.\n"
"5. **Relevance:** Connect it to the position.\n"
"\n"
"## Practice Scenario\n"
"\n"
"In this roleplay, the AI recruiter will interview you for your desired "
"position. When you provide a CV or vacancy description, the questions will "
"be adapted to your experience and the role.\n"
"\n"
"During the interview, try to:\n"
"\n"
"- Give a focused professional introduction.\n"
"- Explain why you want the role.\n"
"- Use the STAR method.\n"
"- Support strengths with examples.\n"
"- Discuss mistakes and weaknesses honestly.\n"
"- Explain your personal contribution.\n"
"- Ask for clarification when necessary.\n"
"- Ask thoughtful questions.\n"
"- Close the interview professionally.\n"
"\n"
"Treat it like a real interview. The recruiter may ask follow-up questions "
"or challenge vague answers. Detailed feedback will be provided after the "
"interview so the conversation remains realistic."
msgstr ""
"En vellykket jobsamtale handler ikke om at memorere perfekte svar. Det "
"handler om at hjælpe intervieweren med at forstå, hvad du kan gøre, hvordan "
"du arbejder, og hvorfor din erfaring er relevant.\n"
"\n"
"Stærke svar er klare, specifikke og understøttet af virkelige eksempler. Du "
"behøver ikke kompliceret ordforråd eller overdreven formelt sprog. Fokuser "
"på at forklare din erfaring på en struktureret og overbevisende måde.\n"
"\n"
"## Forbered dig før interviewet\n"
"\n"
"Før interviewet, gennemgå:\n"
"\n"
"- Rollen og dens hovedansvar\n"
"- De vigtigste krav\n"
"- Virksomhedens produkter og kunder\n"
"- Din mest relevante erfaring\n"
"- To eller tre præstationer\n"
"- Eksempler på problemer du har løst\n"
"- Spørgsmål du ønsker at stille\n"
"\n"
"Forbind din erfaring med stillingen. Hvis teamwork er vigtigt, forbered et "
"teamwork-eksempel. Hvis rollen kræver lederskab, tænk på en tid, hvor du "
"tog ansvar eller hjalp et team med at opnå fremskridt.\n"
"\n"
"Du behøver ikke at matche alle krav. Vær klar til at forklare, hvordan dine "
"eksisterende færdigheder kan overføres til ukendte ansvar.\n"
"\n"
"## Introducer dig selv\n"
"\n"
"Mange interviews begynder med:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Kan du fortælle mig lidt om dig selv?\"\n"
"\n"
"Giv en kort professionel oversigt, der dækker:\n"
"\n"
"1. Hvad du gør\n"
"2. Din relevante erfaring\n"
"3. Dine stærkeste færdigheder\n"
"4. Hvorfor du ønsker denne rolle\n"
"\n"
"En nyttig struktur er:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Jeg er en [profession] med erfaring inden for [område]. I min nuværende "
"eller seneste rolle havde jeg [ansvar eller præstation]. Mine stærkeste "
"færdigheder inkluderer [færdigheder]. Nu leder jeg efter en mulighed, hvor "
"jeg kan [mål forbundet med stillingen].\"\n"
"\n"
"Eksempel:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Jeg er en frontend-udvikler med fem års erfaring med at bygge "
"webapplikationer. Jeg arbejder hovedsageligt med React og TypeScript og "
"hjælper med at forbedre frontend-arkitektur og automatiseret testning. Nu "
"leder jeg efter en rolle, hvor jeg kan tage mere ejerskab og bidrage til "
"tekniske beslutninger.\"\n"
"\n"
"Hold din introduktion fokuseret. Et eller to minutter er normalt "
"tilstrækkeligt.\n"
"\n"
"## Forklar din motivation\n"
"\n"
"Interviewere kan spørge:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Hvorfor er du interesseret i denne stilling?\"\n"
"- \"Hvorfor vil du arbejde her?\"\n"
"- \"Hvorfor forlader du din nuværende rolle?\"\n"
"\n"
"Forbind tre ting:\n"
"\n"
"- Noget specifikt om rollen eller virksomheden\n"
"- Din relevante erfaring\n"
"- Hvad du ønsker at udvikle næste\n"
"\n"
"Eksempel:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Jeg er interesseret i denne rolle, fordi den kombinerer "
"frontend-udvikling med produktlederskab. Jeg har erfaring med at bygge "
"React-applikationer og forbedre testprocesser, og jeg vil nu gerne deltage "
"mere aktivt i arkitektur- og produktbeslutninger.\"\n"
"\n"
"Undgå at fokusere kun på løn, fjernarbejde, eller at have brug for et "
"hvilket som helst tilgængeligt job.\n"
"\n"
"## Brug STAR Metoden\n"
"\n"
"Til spørgsmål om tidligere erfaringer, brug **STAR**:\n"
"\n"
"- **Situation:** Forklar konteksten.\n"
"- **Task:** Beskriv dit ansvar.\n"
"- **Action:** Forklar, hvad du personligt gjorde.\n"
"- **Result:** Beskriv resultatet og læren.\n"
"\n"
"Eksempel:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Vores checkout-side fejlede ofte på mobile enheder. Jeg undersøgte "
"analytics og genskabte problemet på flere enheder. Jeg opdagede, at to "
"forespørgsler skabte en race condition, ændrede forespørgselsflowet og "
"tilføjede integrationstest. Efter udgivelsen faldt fejl på mobile checkout "
"betydeligt.\"\n"
"\n"
"**Aktion**-sektionen bør normalt indeholde mest detaljer. Interviewere vil "
"forstå din indsats, ikke kun hvad teamet gjorde.\n"
"\n"
"## Gør svarene specifikke\n"
"\n"
"Sammenlign:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Jeg hjalp med at forbedre produktet.\"\n"
"\n"
"Med:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Jeg redesignede onboarding-flowet, forenklede tre trin med designeren, "
"og tilføjede analytics. Andelen af brugere, der gennemførte onboarding steg "
"fra 62% til 78%.\"\n"
"\n"
"Brug præcise tal, når de er meningsfulde. Du kan nævne øget indtjening, "
"reducerede fejl, hurtigere levering, sparet tid, forbedret tilfredshed "
"eller flere gennemførte processer.\n"
"\n"
"Når præcise tal ikke er tilgængelige, beskriv et konkret resultat:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Supportteamet stoppede med at modtage gentagne klager.\"\n"
"- \"Vi gennemførte migrationen uden nedetid.\"\n"
"- \"Løsningen blev taget i brug af to andre teams.\"\n"
"\n"
"Opfind ikke statistik.\n"
"\n"
"## Forklar din indsats\n"
"\n"
"Interviewere kan spørge om dine ansvarsområder, projekter eller rolle inden "
"for et team.\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige sætninger inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Jeg var ansvarlig for…\"\n"
"- \"Mit hovedbidrag var…\"\n"
"- \"Jeg tog ejerskab af…\"\n"
"- \"Jeg arbejdede tæt sammen med…\"\n"
"- \"Teamet leverede projektet, mens jeg fokuserede på…\"\n"
"- \"Jeg var involveret fra planlægning til frigivelse.\"\n"
"\n"
"Brug “vi” for fælles resultater og “jeg” for dine egne handlinger.\n"
"\n"
"## Beskriv styrker med beviser\n"
"\n"
"Vælg styrker, der er relevante for rollen og underbyg dem med eksempler.\n"
"\n"
"I stedet for:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Jeg er en god kommunikator.\"\n"
"\n"
"Prøv:\n"
"\n"
"> \"En af mine styrker er at forklare tekniske beslutninger til "
"ikke-tekniske kolleger. Under vores sidste redesign brugte jeg simple "
"prototyper til at forklare performance-kompromisser til produkt- og "
"design-teams. Dette hjalp os med at blive enige om en løsning uden at "
"forsinke udgivelsen.\"\n"
"\n"
"Mulige styrker inkluderer problemløsning, pålidelighed, kommunikation, "
"tilpasningsevne, lederskab, organisation, teknisk ekspertise og hurtig "
"læring.\n"
"\n"
"## Diskuter en svaghed ærligt\n"
"\n"
"Vælg en reel begrænsning, der ikke gør dig uegnet til rollen. Forklar:\n"
"\n"
"1. Hvad svagheden er\n"
"2. Hvornår den påvirker dig\n"
"3. Hvad du gør ved det\n"
"4. Hvilket fremskridt du har gjort\n"
"\n"
"Eksempel:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Jeg bruger nogle gange for meget tid på at forfine detaljer, før jeg "
"deler mit arbejde. Jeg deler nu tidligere udkast og aftaler det forventede "
"detaljeringsniveau, inden jeg begynder. Dette har hjulpet mig med at få "
"feedback tidligere og arbejde mere effektivt.\"\n"
"\n"
"Undgå forklædte styrker som \"Jeg arbejder for hårdt.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Forklar fejl og fiaskoer\n"
"\n"
"Et godt svar demonstrerer ansvarlighed og læring.\n"
"\n"
"Inkluder:\n"
"\n"
"- Hvad der skete\n"
"- Hvad din rolle var\n"
"- Hvad du skulle have gjort anderledes\n"
"- Hvordan du reducerede påvirkningen\n"
"- Hvad du ændrede efterfølgende\n"
"\n"
"Eksempel:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Jeg undervurderede en datamigration, fordi jeg ikke inkluderede nok tid "
"til at teste med produktionsdata. Jeg rejste risikoen tidligt, reducerede "
"det første udgivelsesscope, og lavede en bedre valideringsplan. Siden da "
"inkluderer jeg validering og rollback-planlægning i migrationsestimater.\"\n"
"\n"
"Skyld ikke på kolleger eller lad som om fejlen ikke havde nogen "
"konsekvenser.\n"
"\n"
"## Tal om konflikt\n"
"\n"
"Når du beskriver en uenighed, forklar:\n"
"\n"
"- Hvad uenigheden handlede om\n"
"- Hvorfor begge sider havde rimelige bekymringer\n"
"- Hvordan du lyttede og forklarede dit synspunkt\n"
"- Hvordan beslutningen blev truffet\n"
"- Hvad der skete efterfølgende\n"
"\n"
"Eksempel:\n"
"\n"
"> \"En designer og jeg var uenige om en animation, der forårsagede "
"performance-problemer på ældre telefoner. Jeg forberedte to prototyper og "
"målte deres ydeevne. Vi valgte en simplere version, der bevarede den "
"vigtigste visuelle effekt.\"\n"
"\n"
"Fokuser på kommunikation og løsning. Undgå at beskrive den anden person som "
"inkompetent eller ufornuftig.\n"
"\n"
"## Forklar hvordan du arbejder\n"
"\n"
"Interviewere kan spørge, hvordan du kommunikerer, beder om hjælp, giver "
"feedback eller håndterer delt ansvar.\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige sætninger inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Jeg holder interessenter informeret ved at…\"\n"
"- \"Jeg foretrækker at rejse risici tidligt.\"\n"
"- \"Når jeg er blokeret, gør jeg først…, og så…\"\n"
"- \"Jeg fokuserer feedback på arbejdet og dets indvirkning.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg sikrer mig, at rollerne er klare, før vi begynder.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg tilpasser detaljeniveauet til personen, jeg taler med.\"\n"
"\n"
"Understøt disse påstande med eksempler.\n"
"\n"
"## Forklar hvordan du prioriterer\n"
"\n"
"Når flere opgaver synes at være presserende:\n"
"\n"
"- Sammenlign deres forretningspåvirkning\n"
"- Tjek deadlines og afhængigheder\n"
"- Diskuter kompromiser\n"
"- Bekræft prioriteter med den relevante person\n"
"- Del arbejdet op i mindre leverancer\n"
"- Kommuniker risici tidligt\n"
"\n"
"Eksempel:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Jeg sammenligner kundeindvirkningen, deadlines og afhængighederne af "
"hver opgave. Jeg bekræfter prioriteter med produkt-ejeren i stedet for at "
"lave antagelser og kommunikerer straks, hvis tidslinjen er i fare.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Besvar hypotetiske spørgsmål\n"
"\n"
"Til ukendte situationer:\n"
"\n"
"1. Afklar situationen.\n"
"2. Identificer målet og begrænsningerne.\n"
"3. Indsamle information.\n"
"4. Overvej mulighederne.\n"
"5. Kommuniker med relevante personer.\n"
"6. Tag aktion.\n"
"7. Gennemgå resultatet.\n"
"\n"
"Du kan stille et afklarende spørgsmål før du svarer:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Ville jeg være ansvarlig for at træffe den endelige beslutning, eller "
"ville jeg rådgive projektlederen?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Vær ærlig om manglende erfaring\n"
"\n"
"Du kan sige:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Jeg har ikke brugt det præcise værktøj, men jeg har arbejdet med et "
"lignende.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg har endnu ingen direkte erfaring på dette område.\"\n"
"- \"Min nærmeste relevante erfaring er…\"\n"
"- \"Jeg ville gå til læring af det ved…\"\n"
"- \"Selvom jeg ikke har gjort det professionelt, har jeg brugt det i et "
"personligt projekt.\"\n"
"\n"
"En nyttig struktur er:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Jeg har ikke gjort X direkte, men jeg har erfaring med Y, som bruger "
"lignende principper. Jeg lærte Z hurtigt i min tidligere rolle, så jeg "
"ville bruge en lignende tilgang her.\"\n"
"\n"
"Overdriv ikke din erfaring.\n"
"\n"
"## Forklar karriereskift og arbejdsafbrydelser\n"
"\n"
"Hold forklaringen ærlig, kortfattet og fokuseret på fremtiden.\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige sætninger inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Jeg tog en pause fra arbejde for at…\"\n"
"- \"Min stilling blev påvirket af omstrukturering.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg besluttede at skifte retning fordi…\"\n"
"- \"I den periode fokuserede jeg på…\"\n"
"- \"Erfaringen hjalp mig med at afklare, at jeg ønsker at…\"\n"
"\n"
"Du behøver ikke at afsløre dybt personlige oplysninger.\n"
"\n"
"## Diskutér lønforventninger\n"
"\n"
"Du kan give et interval:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Baseret på ansvaret og min erfaring, sigter jeg efter en bruttoløn "
"mellem X og Y. Jeg overvejer også den fulde kompensationspakke og omfanget "
"af rollen.\"\n"
"\n"
"Du kan også spørge:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Kunne I dele det budgetterede løninterval?\"\n"
"- \"Inkluderer tallet bonusser?\"\n"
"- \"Er der regelmæssige lønrevisioner?\"\n"
"- \"Er der fleksibilitet afhængigt af de endelige ansvarsområder?\"\n"
"\n"
"Undersøg lokale markedsrater og overvej løn, fordele, ferie, arbejdsvilkår "
"og udviklingsmuligheder.\n"
"\n"
"## Stil spørgsmål til sidst\n"
"\n"
"Forbered flere overvejede spørgsmål.\n"
"\n"
"### Om rollen\n"
"\n"
"- \"Hvordan ville succes se ud i de første tre måneder?\"\n"
"- \"Hvad er de vigtigste problemer, denne person skal løse?\"\n"
"- \"Hvorfor er stillingen i øjeblikket åben?\"\n"
"- \"Hvad er de største udfordringer i denne rolle?\"\n"
"\n"
"### Om teamet\n"
"\n"
"- \"Hvordan er teamet struktureret?\"\n"
"- \"Hvem ville jeg arbejde tæt med?\"\n"
"- \"Hvordan træffes vigtige beslutninger?\"\n"
"- \"Hvordan deles feedbacken i teamet?\"\n"
"\n"
"### Om proceduren\n"
"\n"
"- \"Hvad er de næste trin?\"\n"
"- \"Er der noget i min erfaring, du gerne vil have uddybet?\"\n"
"- \"Hvornår forventer I at træffe beslutning?\"\n"
"\n"
"Brug denne mulighed til at vurdere rollen, ikke kun til at demonstrere "
"interesse.\n"
"\n"
"## Bed om afklaring\n"
"\n"
"Du behøver ikke svare straks, når et spørgsmål er uklart.\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige sætninger inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Kan du præcisere, hvad du mener?\"\n"
"- \"Vil du have et eksempel fra min nuværende rolle?\"\n"
"- \"Kan du gentage spørgsmålet, tak?\"\n"
"- \"Må jeg tage et øjeblik til at tænke?\"\n"
"- \"Lad mig sikre mig, at jeg forstod korrekt.\"\n"
"\n"
"En kort pause er bedre end et spredt svar.\n"
"\n"
"## Hold svarene fokuserede\n"
"\n"
"De fleste svar bør tage mellem et og tre minutter.\n"
"\n"
"En nyttig struktur er:\n"
"\n"
"1. Begynd med dit hovedpunkt.\n"
"2. Giv et relevant eksempel.\n"
"3. Forklar dine handlinger og resultatet.\n"
"4. Stop og giv mulighed for et opfølgningsspørgsmål.\n"
"\n"
"En stærk åbning kunne være:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Ja. Det bedste eksempel er et migrationsprojekt, jeg ledede sidste "
"år.\"\n"
"\n"
"Hvis dit svar bliver for langt, sig:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Hovedresultatet var…\"\n"
"- \"For at opsummere…\"\n"
"- \"Den vigtigste lære var…\"\n"
"\n"
"## Kommuniker naturligt på et andet sprog\n"
"\n"
"Perfekt grammatik er ikke påkrævet. Prioritér:\n"
"\n"
"- Klar struktur\n"
"- Specifikke eksempler\n"
"- Forståelig udtale\n"
"- Relevant information\n"
"- Omhyggelig lytning\n"
"- At bede om afklaring\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige sætninger inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Hvad jeg mener er…\"\n"
"- \"Lad mig forklare det på en anden måde.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg leder efter det rigtige ord.\"\n"
"- \"Kunne du tale lidt langsommere?\"\n"
"- \"Jeg har brug for et øjeblik til at organisere mit svar.\"\n"
"\n"
"At rette sig roligt er fuldstændig acceptabelt.\n"
"\n"
"## Tips til online interview\n"
"\n"
"Før en video interview:\n"
"\n"
"- Test dit kamera, mikrofon og internetforbindelse.\n"
"- Deltag flere minutter før.\n"
"- Hav dit CV og jobopslaget i nærheden.\n"
"- Luk unødvendige applikationer og notifikationer.\n"
"- Vælg et stille, godt oplyst sted.\n"
"- Hold interviewers kontaktoplysninger tilgængelige.\n"
"\n"
"Hvis der er et teknisk problem, sig:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Jeg er ked af det, lyden skærer ud.\"\n"
"- \"Kunne du gentage den sidste sætning?\"\n"
"- \"Jeg tror, der er en forsinkelse.\"\n"
"- \"Ville du have noget imod, hvis jeg slukkede mit kamera?\"\n"
"- \"Kunne vi genoprette forbindelsen ved hjælp af det samme link?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Afslut professionelt\n"
"\n"
"I slutningen kan du sige:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Tak for din tid.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg nød at lære mere om rollen.\"\n"
"- \"Stillingen lyder tæt forbundet med, hvad jeg gerne vil gøre næste.\"\n"
"- \"Lad mig vide, hvis du har brug for yderligere information.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg ser frem til at høre om de næste trin.\"\n"
"\n"
"Udtryk interesse, tak intervieweren, og bekræft processen.\n"
"\n"
"## En simpel svareformel\n"
"\n"
"For de fleste erfaring-baserede spørgsmål, brug:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Svar:** Giv dit hovedpunkt.\n"
"2. **Eksempel:** Beskriv en relevant situation.\n"
"3. **Handling:** Forklar hvad du gjorde.\n"
"4. **Resultat:** Beskriv resultatet.\n"
"5. **Relevans:** Forbind det til stillingen.\n"
"\n"
"## Øv scenarie\n"
"\n"
"I denne rollespil vil AI rekruttere interviewe dig til din ønskede "
"stilling. Når du giver et CV eller jobbeskrivelse, vil spørgsmålene blive "
"tilpasset til din erfaring og rollen.\n"
"\n"
"Under interviewet, prøv at:\n"
"\n"
"- Give en fokuseret professionel introduktion.\n"
"- Forklare hvorfor du vil have rollen.\n"
"- Brug STAR-metoden.\n"
"- Understøtte styrker med eksempler.\n"
"- Diskutere fejl og svagheder ærligt.\n"
"- Forklare din personlige indsats.\n"
"- Bede om afklaring når nødvendigt.\n"
"- Stille gennemtænkte spørgsmål.\n"
"- Afslutte interviewet professionelt.\n"
"\n"
"Behandl det som et rigtigt interview. Rekruttøren kan stille opfølgende "
"spørgsmål eller udfordre vage svar. Detaljeret feedback vil blive givet "
"efter interviewet, så samtalen forbliver realistisk."

