#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/at-the-grocery-store.ts:354
#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/returning-an-item-in-a-store.ts:22
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid "Shopping"
msgstr "Shopping"

#: src/features/RolePlay/scenarios/at-the-grocery-store.ts:16
#. js-lingui-explicit-id
msgid ""
"Shopping at a grocery store involves many short but useful conversations. "
"You may need to find a product, ask about a price, understand a promotion, "
"check ingredients, or speak with a cashier.\n"
"\n"
"You do not need long or complicated sentences. Clear questions and polite "
"phrases are usually enough.\n"
"\n"
"## How to Ask Where Something Is\n"
"\n"
"When you cannot find a product, you can approach an employee and say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Excuse me, could you help me?”\n"
"- “Where can I find the milk?”\n"
"- “Which aisle is the pasta in?”\n"
"- “Do you know where the rice is?”\n"
"- “I’m looking for olive oil.”\n"
"- “Could you show me where it is?”\n"
"\n"
"An employee may respond with directions such as:\n"
"\n"
"- “It’s in aisle five.”\n"
"- “It’s next to the bread.”\n"
"- “You’ll find it at the back of the store.”\n"
"- “It’s on the top shelf.”\n"
"- “It’s in the refrigerated section.”\n"
"- “Follow me. I’ll show you.”\n"
"\n"
"Useful location words include:\n"
"\n"
"- **Aisle** — a passage between shelves\n"
"- **Shelf** — the surface where products are displayed\n"
"- **Checkout** — the place where you pay\n"
"- **Refrigerated section** — the area for chilled products\n"
"- **Frozen-food section** — the area containing frozen products\n"
"- **Produce section** — the area containing fruit and vegetables\n"
"- **Bakery section** — the area containing bread and baked goods\n"
"\n"
"## Ask Whether a Product Is Available\n"
"\n"
"Sometimes a shelf is empty or the product you need is difficult to find.\n"
"\n"
"You can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Do you have this product?”\n"
"- “Do you sell oat milk?”\n"
"- “Is this item still available?”\n"
"- “Do you have any more in stock?”\n"
"- “When will this be available again?”\n"
"- “Is there another brand you would recommend?”\n"
"- “Do you have a similar product?”\n"
"\n"
"If the product is unavailable, an employee may say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’m afraid it’s out of stock.”\n"
"- “We should have more tomorrow.”\n"
"- “That product has been discontinued.”\n"
"- “We have a similar one from another brand.”\n"
"- “Let me check in the storage room.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Prices\n"
"\n"
"Price labels can sometimes be unclear, especially when several products are "
"displayed together.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “How much is this?”\n"
"- “Could you check the price for me?”\n"
"- “Is this the correct price?”\n"
"- “Is the price per item or per kilogram?”\n"
"- “Does this include tax?”\n"
"- “Why is the price different at the checkout?”\n"
"- “Which one is cheaper?”\n"
"\n"
"You may also hear:\n"
"\n"
"- “It costs three ninety-nine.”\n"
"- “It’s sold by weight.”\n"
"- “The price is per kilogram.”\n"
"- “The discount is applied at the checkout.”\n"
"- “You need a loyalty card to get that price.”\n"
"\n"
"## Understand Promotions and Discounts\n"
"\n"
"Stores often use promotional language that may be confusing.\n"
"\n"
"Common offers include:\n"
"\n"
"- **Buy one, get one free**\n"
"- **Two for five**\n"
"- **Twenty percent off**\n"
"- **Reduced price**\n"
"- **Special offer**\n"
"- **Member price**\n"
"- **Loyalty-card price**\n"
"- **Clearance**\n"
"- **Valid until Friday**\n"
"\n"
"Questions you can ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “Is this product on sale?”\n"
"- “How does this promotion work?”\n"
"- “Do I need to buy two?”\n"
"- “Do I need a loyalty card?”\n"
"- “Is the discount applied automatically?”\n"
"- “When does the promotion end?”\n"
"- “Can I combine this offer with another discount?”\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “The label says two for five. Can I buy only one?”\n"
"\n"
"The employee may explain:\n"
"\n"
"> “Yes, but one item will cost three.”\n"
"\n"
"## Compare Products\n"
"\n"
"You may want to compare brands, sizes, ingredients, or prices.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “What is the difference between these two?”\n"
"- “Which one is more popular?”\n"
"- “Which one is better value?”\n"
"- “Is there a cheaper option?”\n"
"- “Do you have a larger size?”\n"
"- “Does this come in a smaller package?”\n"
"- “Which brand would you recommend?”\n"
"- “Is there a store-brand version?”\n"
"\n"
"A useful phrase is:\n"
"\n"
"> “I’m looking for something similar, but less expensive.”\n"
"\n"
"You can also explain your priorities:\n"
"\n"
"- “I need something without added sugar.”\n"
"- “I’m looking for a high-protein option.”\n"
"- “I’d prefer something organic.”\n"
"- “I need a product that will last several days.”\n"
"- “I’m looking for the best value, not necessarily the cheapest product.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Ingredients and Dietary Needs\n"
"\n"
"Checking ingredients is especially important if you have allergies or "
"dietary preferences.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Does this contain nuts?”\n"
"- “Is this gluten-free?”\n"
"- “Is this suitable for vegetarians?”\n"
"- “Is this vegan?”\n"
"- “Does this contain dairy?”\n"
"- “Is there any added sugar?”\n"
"- “Where can I find lactose-free products?”\n"
"- “Do you have a dairy-free alternative?”\n"
"\n"
"You can also say:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’m allergic to peanuts.”\n"
"- “I cannot eat gluten.”\n"
"- “I’m looking for something without dairy.”\n"
"- “Could you help me check the ingredients?”\n"
"\n"
"For serious allergies, always read the package carefully. A store employee "
"may help you find information, but they may not be able to guarantee that a "
"product is completely allergen-free.\n"
"\n"
"## Buy Fruit, Vegetables, Meat, or Cheese\n"
"\n"
"Some products are sold by weight rather than by package.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “I’d like one kilogram of apples, please.”\n"
"- “Could I have half a kilogram of tomatoes?”\n"
"- “I’d like three hundred grams of cheese.”\n"
"- “Could you give me six slices?”\n"
"- “Can I have two chicken breasts?”\n"
"- “That’s enough, thank you.”\n"
"\n"
"The employee may ask:\n"
"\n"
"- “How much would you like?”\n"
"- “Is this amount okay?”\n"
"- “Would you like it sliced?”\n"
"- “Would you like anything else?”\n"
"- “Do you need a bag?”\n"
"\n"
"You can respond:\n"
"\n"
"- “A little more, please.”\n"
"- “A little less, please.”\n"
"- “That amount is perfect.”\n"
"- “Could you slice it thinly?”\n"
"- “No, that’s everything.”\n"
"\n"
"## Ask About Product Freshness\n"
"\n"
"You may want to check whether food is fresh or how long it will last.\n"
"\n"
"Useful questions include:\n"
"\n"
"- “When does this expire?”\n"
"- “What is the use-by date?”\n"
"- “Was this baked today?”\n"
"- “Is this fresh?”\n"
"- “How long will this keep?”\n"
"- “Should I store this in the refrigerator?”\n"
"- “Can this be frozen?”\n"
"\n"
"Common date labels include:\n"
"\n"
"- **Best before** — the product may lose quality after this date\n"
"- **Use by** — the product should normally be consumed before this date\n"
"- **Packed on** — the date the product was packaged\n"
"- **Sell by** — a date mainly used by the store\n"
"\n"
"## Handle Problems with a Product\n"
"\n"
"You may notice that an item is damaged, open, expired, or incorrectly "
"labelled.\n"
"\n"
"You can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “This package is damaged.”\n"
"- “This bottle is leaking.”\n"
"- “I think this product has expired.”\n"
"- “The seal is broken.”\n"
"- “This item was on the wrong shelf.”\n"
"- “Could I exchange this for another one?”\n"
"- “Could someone check this product?”\n"
"\n"
"Stay polite and explain the problem clearly.\n"
"\n"
"For example:\n"
"\n"
"> “Excuse me, this carton is leaking. Could I replace it?”\n"
"\n"
"## Speak at the Checkout\n"
"\n"
"When you reach the checkout, the cashier may ask several common questions:\n"
"\n"
"- “Did you find everything you needed?”\n"
"- “Do you have a loyalty card?”\n"
"- “Would you like a bag?”\n"
"- “Do you need a receipt?”\n"
"- “Are you paying by cash or card?”\n"
"- “Would you like to donate to charity?”\n"
"- “Do you need help packing?”\n"
"\n"
"Useful answers include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Yes, I found everything, thank you.”\n"
"- “No, I couldn’t find one item.”\n"
"- “I don’t have a loyalty card.”\n"
"- “Yes, one bag, please.”\n"
"- “No bag, thank you.”\n"
"- “I’ll pay by card.”\n"
"- “Could I have the receipt, please?”\n"
"- “Could I pay separately for these items?”\n"
"\n"
"## Understand Checkout Instructions\n"
"\n"
"When paying by card, you may hear:\n"
"\n"
"- “Please insert your card.”\n"
"- “You can tap your card.”\n"
"- “Please enter your PIN.”\n"
"- “Your payment was declined.”\n"
"- “Would you like to try again?”\n"
"- “Please remove your card.”\n"
"- “The payment has gone through.”\n"
"\n"
"If something goes wrong, you can say:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could I try another card?”\n"
"- “Can I pay in cash instead?”\n"
"- “I think I was charged twice.”\n"
"- “Could you check the total?”\n"
"- “The price on the shelf was different.”\n"
"- “Could you remove this item, please?”\n"
"\n"
"## Use Self-Checkout\n"
"\n"
"At a self-checkout, you may need to ask an employee for help.\n"
"\n"
"Useful phrases include:\n"
"\n"
"- “Could you help me with the self-checkout?”\n"
"- “The machine is not scanning this item.”\n"
"- “It says there is an unexpected item.”\n"
"- “How do I weigh the vegetables?”\n"
"- “Where do I enter the product number?”\n"
"- “How can I remove an item?”\n"
"- “The machine has not printed my receipt.”\n"
"\n"
"You may see or hear instructions such as:\n"
"\n"
"- “Scan your first item.”\n"
"- “Place the item in the bagging area.”\n"
"- “Select your payment method.”\n"
"- “Approval needed.”\n"
"- “Please wait for assistance.”\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Grocery Store Conversation\n"
"\n"
"A typical interaction may look like this:\n"
"\n"
"> **Customer:** Excuse me, could you help me find oat milk?  \n"
"> **Employee:** Of course. It’s in aisle six, next to the regular milk.  \n"
"> **Customer:** Thank you. Do you have an unsweetened version?  \n"
"> **Employee:** Yes, we have two brands. This one is currently on sale.  \n"
"> **Customer:** How does the promotion work?  \n"
"> **Employee:** It’s twenty percent off if you have a loyalty card.  \n"
"> **Customer:** I don’t have one. Is there a cheaper alternative?  \n"
"> **Employee:** Yes, the store-brand version is less expensive.  \n"
"> **Customer:** Great. Could you show me where it is?\n"
"\n"
"## A Simple Shopping Formula\n"
"\n"
"When you need help, use this structure:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Get attention:** “Excuse me, could you help me?”\n"
"2. **Explain what you need:** “I’m looking for brown rice.”\n"
"3. **Ask a specific question:** “Which aisle is it in?”\n"
"4. **Clarify the answer:** “Did you say aisle seven?”\n"
"5. **Thank the employee:** “Great, thank you for your help.”\n"
"\n"
"## Practice Scenario\n"
"\n"
"In this roleplay, you are shopping at FreshMart. The AI employee will help "
"you find products, explain prices and promotions, and answer questions "
"about the store.\n"
"\n"
"During the conversation, try to:\n"
"\n"
"- Ask where at least one product is located.\n"
"- Ask about a price or promotion.\n"
"- Compare two products.\n"
"- Ask about an ingredient or dietary requirement.\n"
"- Respond to one small problem, such as an unavailable product or unclear "
"price.\n"
"- Complete the purchase or end the interaction politely.\n"
"\n"
"Focus on communicating your needs clearly. You do not need perfect grammar "
"to have a successful conversation in a grocery store."
msgstr ""
"At handle indkøb i en købmand involverer mange korte, men nyttige samtaler. "
"Du kan have brug for at finde et produkt, spørge om en pris, forstå en "
"kampagne, tjekke ingredienser eller tale med en kasserer.\n"
"\n"
"Du behøver ikke lange eller komplicerede sætninger. Klare spørgsmål og "
"høflige vendinger er normalt nok.\n"
"\n"
"## Hvordan man spørger, hvor noget er\n"
"\n"
"Når du ikke kan finde et produkt, kan du henvende dig til en medarbejder og "
"sige:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Undskyld, kunne du hjælpe mig?\"\n"
"- \"Hvor kan jeg finde mælken?\"\n"
"- \"Hvilken gang er pastaen i?\"\n"
"- \"Ved du, hvor risene er?\"\n"
"- \"Jeg leder efter olivenolie.\"\n"
"- \"Kunne du vise mig, hvor det er?\"\n"
"\n"
"En medarbejder kan svare med vejledninger såsom:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Det er i gang fem.\"\n"
"- \"Det er ved siden af brødet.\"\n"
"- \"Du finder det i bagerst i butikken.\"\n"
"- \"Det er på den øverste hylde.\"\n"
"- \"Det er i kølesektionen.\"\n"
"- \"Følg mig. Jeg skal vise dig.\"\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige placeringsord inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- **Gang** — en passage mellem hylder\n"
"- **Hylde** — overfladen hvor produkter er udstillet\n"
"- **Kasse** — stedet hvor du betaler\n"
"- **Kølesektion** — området for nedkølede produkter\n"
"- **Frost-sektion** — området indeholdende frostvarer\n"
"- **Frugt og grønt-sektion** — området med frugt og grøntsager\n"
"- **Bageri-sektion** — området med brød og bagværk\n"
"\n"
"## Spørg om et produkt er tilgængeligt\n"
"\n"
"Nogle gange er en hylde tom, eller produktet du har brug for, er svært at "
"finde.\n"
"\n"
"Du kan spørge:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Har I dette produkt?\"\n"
"- \"Sælger I havremælk?\"\n"
"- \"Er denne vare stadig tilgængelig?\"\n"
"- \"Har I flere på lager?\"\n"
"- \"Hvornår vil dette være tilgængeligt igen?\"\n"
"- \"Er der et andet mærke, du vil anbefale?\"\n"
"- \"Har I et lignende produkt?\"\n"
"\n"
"Hvis produktet ikke er tilgængeligt, kan en medarbejder sige:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Jeg er bange for, at det er udsolgt.\"\n"
"- \"Vi skulle have flere i morgen.\"\n"
"- \"Det produkt er udgået.\"\n"
"- \"Vi har en lignende fra et andet mærke.\"\n"
"- \"Lad mig tjekke på lageret.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Spørg om priser\n"
"\n"
"Prismærker kan sommetider være uklare, især når flere produkter er "
"udstillet sammen.\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige spørgsmål inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Hvor meget koster dette?\"\n"
"- \"Kunne du tjekke prisen for mig?\"\n"
"- \"Er dette den korrekte pris?\"\n"
"- \"Er prisen per styk eller per kilogram?\"\n"
"- \"Inkluderer dette moms?\"\n"
"- \"Hvorfor er prisen anderledes ved kassen?\"\n"
"- \"Hvilken er billigere?\"\n"
"\n"
"Du kan også høre:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Det koster tre nioghalvfems.\"\n"
"- \"Det sælges efter vægt.\"\n"
"- \"Prisen er per kilogram.\"\n"
"- \"Rabat anvendes ved kassen.\"\n"
"- \"Du skal bruge et loyalitetskort for at få den pris.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Forstå kampagner og rabatter\n"
"\n"
"Butikker bruger ofte kampagnesprog, der kan være forvirrende.\n"
"\n"
"Almindelige tilbud inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- **Køb en, få en gratis**\n"
"- **To for fem**\n"
"- **Tyve procent rabat**\n"
"- **Nedsat pris**\n"
"- **Særtilbud**\n"
"- **Medlemspris**\n"
"- **Loyalitetskort pris**\n"
"- **Udsalg**\n"
"- **Gyldig til fredag**\n"
"\n"
"Spørgsmål du kan stille:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Er dette produkt på tilbud?\"\n"
"- \"Hvordan fungerer denne kampagne?\"\n"
"- \"Skal jeg købe to?\"\n"
"- \"Skal jeg bruge et loyalitetskort?\"\n"
"- \"Anvendes rabatten automatisk?\"\n"
"- \"Hvornår slutter tilbuddet?\"\n"
"- \"Kan jeg kombinere dette tilbud med en anden rabat?\"\n"
"\n"
"For eksempel:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Labelen siger to for fem. Kan jeg købe kun én?\"\n"
"\n"
"Medarbejderen kan forklare:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Ja, men ét stykke vil koste tre.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Sammenlign produkter\n"
"\n"
"Du vil muligvis sammenligne mærker, størrelser, ingredienser eller priser.\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige spørgsmål inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Hvad er forskellen mellem disse to?\"\n"
"- \"Hvilken er mere populær?\"\n"
"- \"Hvilken er bedre værdi?\"\n"
"- \"Er der en billigere mulighed?\"\n"
"- \"Har du en større størrelse?\"\n"
"- \"Kommer dette i en mindre pakke?\"\n"
"- \"Hvilket mærke vil du anbefale?\"\n"
"- \"Er der en butiksudgave?\"\n"
"\n"
"En nyttig vending er:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Jeg leder efter noget lignende, men mindre dyrt.\"\n"
"\n"
"Du kan også forklare dine prioriteter:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Jeg har brug for noget uden tilsat sukker.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg leder efter en højproteinkilde.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg vil foretrække noget økologisk.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg har brug for et produkt, der holder i flere dage.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg leder efter den bedste værdi, ikke nødvendigvis det billigste "
"produkt.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Spørg om ingredienser og kostbehov\n"
"\n"
"At tjekke ingredienser er især vigtigt, hvis du har allergier eller "
"kostpræferencer.\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige spørgsmål inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Indeholder dette nødder?\"\n"
"- \"Er dette glutenfrit?\"\n"
"- \"Er dette egnet for vegetarer?\"\n"
"- \"Er dette vegansk?\"\n"
"- \"Indeholder dette mejeriprodukter?\"\n"
"- \"Er der tilsat sukker?\"\n"
"- \"Hvor kan jeg finde laktosefri produkter?\"\n"
"- \"Har I et mælkefrit alternativ?\"\n"
"\n"
"Du kan også sige:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Jeg er allergisk over for peanuts.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg kan ikke tåle gluten.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg leder efter noget uden mejeri.\"\n"
"- \"Kunne du hjælpe mig med at tjekke ingredienserne?\"\n"
"\n"
"For alvorlige allergier skal du altid læse pakken omhyggeligt. En "
"butiksmedarbejder kan hjælpe dig med at finde information, men de kan måske "
"ikke garantere, at et produkt er helt allergenfrit.\n"
"\n"
"## Køb frugt, grøntsager, kød eller ost\n"
"\n"
"Nogle produkter sælges efter vægt snarere end i pakker.\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige vendinger inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Jeg vil gerne have et kilogram æbler, tak.\"\n"
"- \"Kunne jeg få et halvt kilogram tomater?\"\n"
"- \"Jeg vil gerne have tre hundrede gram ost.\"\n"
"- \"Kunne du give mig seks skiver?\"\n"
"- \"Kan jeg få to kyllingebryst?\"\n"
"- \"Det er nok, tak.\"\n"
"\n"
"Medarbejderen kan spørge:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Hvor meget vil du have?\"\n"
"- \"Er denne mængde okay?\"\n"
"- \"Vil du have det skåret?\"\n"
"- \"Ønsker du noget andet?\"\n"
"- \"Har du brug for en pose?\"\n"
"\n"
"Du kan svare:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Lidt mere, tak.\"\n"
"- \"Lidt mindre, tak.\"\n"
"- \"Den mængde er perfekt.\"\n"
"- \"Kunne du skære det tyndt?\"\n"
"- \"Nej, det er alt.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Spørg om produktets friskhed\n"
"\n"
"Du vil måske tjekke, om mad er frisk, eller hvor længe den vil holde.\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige spørgsmål inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Hvornår udløber dette?\"\n"
"- \"Hvad er sidste anvendelsesdato?\"\n"
"- \"Er dette bagt i dag?\"\n"
"- \"Er dette friskt?\"\n"
"- \"Hvor længe vil dette holde?\"\n"
"- \"Skal jeg opbevare dette i køleskabet?\"\n"
"- \"Kan dette fryses?\"\n"
"\n"
"Almindelige datomærkater inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- **Bedst før** — produktet kan miste kvalitet efter denne dato\n"
"- **Sidste anvendelsesdato** — produktet bør normalt forbruges inden denne "
"dato\n"
"- **Pakket den** — datoen, hvor produktet blev pakket\n"
"- **Salgsdato** — en dato primært brugt af butikken\n"
"\n"
"## Håndter problemer med et produkt\n"
"\n"
"Du kan bemærke, at en vare er beskadiget, åbnet, udløbet eller forkert "
"mærket.\n"
"\n"
"Du kan sige:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Denne pakke er beskadiget.\"\n"
"- \"Denne flaske lækker.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg tror, dette produkt er udløbet.\"\n"
"- \"Forseglingen er brudt.\"\n"
"- \"Denne vare var på den forkerte hylde.\"\n"
"- \"Kunne jeg bytte dette for et andet?\"\n"
"- \"Kunne nogen tjekke dette produkt?\"\n"
"\n"
"Forbliv høflig og forklar problemet klart.\n"
"\n"
"For eksempel:\n"
"\n"
"> \"Undskyld mig, denne karton lækker. Kunne jeg erstatte den?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Tal ved kassen\n"
"\n"
"Når du når kassen, kan kassemedarbejderen stille flere almindelige "
"spørgsmål:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Fandt du alt, hvad du havde brug for?\"\n"
"- \"Har du et loyalitetskort?\"\n"
"- \"Vil du gerne have en pose?\"\n"
"- \"Har du brug for en kvittering?\"\n"
"- \"Betaler du kontant eller med kort?\"\n"
"- \"Vil du donere til velgørenhed?\"\n"
"- \"Har du brug for hjælp med at pakke?\"\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige svar inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Ja, jeg fandt alt, tak.\"\n"
"- \"Nej, jeg kunne ikke finde en vare.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg har ikke et loyalitetskort.\"\n"
"- \"Ja, en pose, tak.\"\n"
"- \"Ingen pose, tak.\"\n"
"- \"Jeg betaler med kort.\"\n"
"- \"Må jeg få kvitteringen, tak?\"\n"
"- \"Kunne jeg betale separat for disse varer?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Forstå instruktioner ved kassen\n"
"\n"
"Når du betaler med kort, kan du høre:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Indsæt venligst dit kort.\"\n"
"- \"Du kan tappe dit kort.\"\n"
"- \"Indtast venligst din PIN-kode.\"\n"
"- \"Din betaling blev afvist.\"\n"
"- \"Vil du prøve igen?\"\n"
"- \"Fjern venligst dit kort.\"\n"
"- \"Betalingen er gået igennem.\"\n"
"\n"
"Hvis noget går galt, kan du sige:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Kunne jeg prøve et andet kort?\"\n"
"- \"Kan jeg betale kontant i stedet?\"\n"
"- \"Jeg tror, jeg blev opkrævet to gange.\"\n"
"- \"Kunne du tjekke totalen?\"\n"
"- \"Prisen på hylden var anderledes.\"\n"
"- \"Kunne du fjerne denne vare, tak?\"\n"
"\n"
"## Brug selvbetjeningskasse\n"
"\n"
"Ved en selvbetjeningskasse kan du have brug for at bede en medarbejder om "
"hjælp.\n"
"\n"
"Nyttige vendinger inkluderer:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Kunne du hjælpe mig med selvbetjeningskassen?\"\n"
"- \"Maskinen scanner ikke denne vare.\"\n"
"- \"Den siger, der er en uventet vare.\"\n"
"- \"Hvordan vejer jeg grøntsagerne?\"\n"
"- \"Hvor indtaster jeg produktnummeret?\"\n"
"- \"Hvordan kan jeg fjerne en vare?\"\n"
"- \"Maskinen har ikke printet min kvittering.\"\n"
"\n"
"Du kan se eller høre instruktioner såsom:\n"
"\n"
"- \"Scan din første vare.\"\n"
"- \"Placer varen i poseområdet.\"\n"
"- \"Vælg din betalingsmetode.\"\n"
"- \"Godkendelse påkrævet.\"\n"
"- \"Vent venligst på hjælp.\"\n"
"\n"
"## En simpel samtale i en købmand\n"
"\n"
"En typisk interaktion kan se sådan ud:\n"
"\n"
"> **Kunde:** Undskyld mig, kunne du hjælpe mig med at finde havremælk?  \n"
"> **Medarbejder:** Selvfølgelig. Det er i gang seks, ved siden af den "
"almindelige mælk.  \n"
"> **Kunde:** Tak. Har du en usødet version?  \n"
"> **Medarbejder:** Ja, vi har to mærker. Dette er i øjeblikket på tilbud.  \n"
"> **Kunde:** Hvordan fungerer kampagnen?  \n"
"> **Medarbejder:** Det er tyve procent rabat, hvis du har et "
"loyalitetskort.  \n"
"> **Kunde:** Jeg har ikke et. Er der et billigere alternativ?  \n"
"> **Medarbejder:** Ja, butiksudgaven er mindre dyr.  \n"
"> **Kunde:** Fremragende. Kunne du vise mig, hvor det er?\n"
"\n"
"## En simpel shoppingformel\n"
"\n"
"Når du har brug for hjælp, brug denne struktur:\n"
"\n"
"1. **Få opmærksomhed:** \"Undskyld mig, kunne du hjælpe mig?\"\n"
"2. **Forklar hvad du har brug for:** \"Jeg leder efter brune ris.\"\n"
"3. **Stil et specifikt spørgsmål:** \"Hvilken gang er det i?\"\n"
"4. **Præciser svaret:** \"Sagde du gang syv?\"\n"
"5. **Tak medarbejderen:** \"Fint, tak for din hjælp.\"\n"
"\n"
"## Øvelsesscenarie\n"
"\n"
"I denne rollespil er du ved at handle i FreshMart. AI-medarbejderen vil "
"hjælpe dig med at finde produkter, forklare priser og kampagner og besvare "
"spørgsmål om butikken.\n"
"\n"
"Under samtalen skal du prøve at:\n"
"\n"
"- Spørge hvor mindst ét produkt er placeret.\n"
"- Spørge om en pris eller kampagne.\n"
"- Sammenligne to produkter.\n"
"- Spørge om en ingrediens eller kostkrav.\n"
"- Reagere på et lille problem, såsom et utilgængeligt produkt eller uklar "
"pris.\n"
"- Fuldføre købet eller afslutte interaktionen høfligt.\n"
"\n"
"Fokusér på at kommunikere dine behov klart. Du behøver ikke perfekt "
"grammatik for at have en vellykket samtale i en købmand."

